The third was taller than the others: his hair was long and gleaming
and on his helm was a crown.  In his one hand he held a long sword,
and in the other a knife; both the knife and the hand that held it
glowed with a pale light.  He sprang forward and bore down on Frodo.

    At that moment Frodo threw himself forward on the ground, and he heard
himself crying aloud: `O Elbereth! Gilthoniel!'  At the same time he
